# Phase 3 — SSH Service & Remote Access

## Objective
Configure and verify the SSH service so the system can accept secure remote access.

## Lab Tasks

### 1. Review the Company Directory Structure
```bash
ls /opt/company
```

### 2. Install OpenSSH Server
```bash
sudo apt install openssh-server
```

### 3. Enable and Start the SSH Service
```bash
sudo systemctl enable --now ssh
```

### 4. Verify SSH Is Running
```bash
systemctl is-active ssh
```

### 5. Test SSH Access Locally
```bash
ssh localhost
```

### 6. Confirm the Active User
```bash
whoami
```

## Notes
- Ensure the SSH service is enabled before testing remote access.
- `ssh localhost` validates local SSH connectivity.
- `whoami` confirms the identity of the logged-in user.
